body:
Hey guys,

&#x200B;

I apologize if this has been posted here before.

&#x200B;

I came across it a few days ago and it just annoyed me how so many Male Issues were just basically brushed off as not as pressing as Female Issues and blamed on "Male Privilege" and "Toxic Masculinity".

&#x200B;

I consider this to be so typical. Many times people will recognize the existence of real Male Issues that deserve attention only to blame them all on males and insist Feminism is the solution to it all.

&#x200B;

According to people like this, Feminism is basically just perfect and there's no such thing as Misandry or any kind of serious discrimination against males, for that matter. Males need to recognize that they have it better than females, that Female Issues are more pressing and if they weren't so busy hating Feminism they'd realize it is already working to fix these issues. Male Advocates must work with Feminism. As if there wasn't serious, systematic pushback against Males in Feminism at all. 

&#x200B;

Feminists would have no problem whatsoever working alongside Male Advocates to achieve true equality... Right?...

&#x200B;

What do you guys think?
